  "body": "MAINLINE-026 complete as a QUESTIONABLE elastic-model study. The frequency-6 frame has 362 joints and 1080 arcs. Rigid-joint linear lambda converges to 6.46522 versus 011b’s 6.12764; representative low modes are global lattice modes. Freely rolling ball pins have 1080 zero-strain member-roll mechanisms, so no positive pressure reserve is established without film or anti-roll stiffness.\n\nRefined nonlinear limits are 5.10740 perfect, 4.95038 for 10 mm joint offsets, 5.08261 for 2.04 mm member crookedness, and 4.53958 for the 10 mm first-mode imperfection. Knockdowns are 0.702–0.790 against discrete perfect linear, or 0.741–0.834 against 011b’s continuum; mesh changes are below 0.7%. These prescribed elastic cases do not validate design k=0.2 or 0.4.\n\nTriangular tributary loading is ps/(2sqrt(3)), not the inherited local ps/2. Discrete mass exceeds inherited lift by 61.40 kg. The inherited wall screen reaches nominal unity near lambda 2.03; computed elastic-limit axial stresses exceed the typical compression strength. No certification.\n\nCode, modes, figures, runtimes, four passing verification suites and 12 NFI rows are pinned through the 263-file manifest. Rejected tangent linearization, replaced diagnostics, one memory-cap failure and one recovered outer receipt are disclosed. All 30 own admissions ended/released; no live work. Stop and file; robotics sends the next job.",
